---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import StatusPill from '../../components/StatusPill.astro';
import { sitePath } from '../../lib/siteUrl';
---

<Layout
  title="Precision Editing"
  description="Exact nudges, scoped snapping, explicit alignment references, and predictable distribution for Varve design work."
>
  <div class="container-custom">
    <main class="precision-page">
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href={sitePath('/features')}>Features</a> / Precision Editing
      </nav>

      <header class="page-hero">
        <StatusPill status="available" />
        <h1>Place things precisely without fighting the canvas.</h1>
        <p>
          Varve separates exact movement from magnetic help and one-shot arrangement. That means
          the command you chose remains the command you get, even in a transformed, multi-page
          document.
        </p>
      </header>

      <section class="hero-card site-card site-card--surface" aria-labelledby="hero-card-title">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">A quieter precision loop</p>
          <h2 id="hero-card-title">Intent → resolve → explain.</h2>
          <p>
            Pointer movement keeps the unsnapped proposal, resolves one common correction for a
            selection, and exposes the relationship through a guide. Keyboard movement stays exact
            and independent. Alignment and distribution calculate from world geometry, then persist
            through each node's parent transform.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="flow" aria-label="Precision editing stages">
          <div><span>01</span><strong>Intent</strong><small>Pointer proposal or exact amount</small></div>
          <div class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
          <div class="flow-accent"><span>02</span><strong>Resolve</strong><small>Scoped targets and references</small></div>
          <div class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
          <div><span>03</span><strong>Verify</strong><small>Guides, values, and one undo step</small></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="capabilities" aria-labelledby="capabilities-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">What is available</p>
        <h2 id="capabilities-title">Small controls with dependable consequences.</h2>
        <div class="capability-grid">
          <article><h3>Fractional nudges</h3><p>Set independent small and big amounts, including positive fractions, in Settings. Existing fractional positions remain fractional.</p></article>
          <article><h3>Scoped snap help</h3><p>Set a 1–32 CSS-pixel tolerance and choose object geometry, page/frame bounds, or ruler/layout guides in Inspector → Document → Snapping. Moving roots are not their own targets.</p></article>
          <article><h3>Stable bypass</h3><p>Hold Ctrl or Cmd during a pointer gesture to bypass magnetic assistance without losing the pointer-to-object relationship.</p></article>
          <article><h3>Explicit references</h3><p>Align to the selection, frame, page, or visible key object. The key object stays put and feedback names the reference used.</p></article>
          <article><h3>Honest spacing modes</h3><p>Equal gaps, equal centers, fixed gap, and Tidy Up are distinct. Fixed gap remains available for two objects; equal-gap distribution accounts for unequal sizes.</p></article>
          <article><h3>Safe history</h3><p>Completed arrangement and movement gestures commit once. Escape, capture loss, and cancellation clear previews or restore the starting geometry.</p></article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="why" aria-labelledby="why-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">Designed around real failure modes</p>
        <h2 id="why-title">No mystery jumps, distant targets, or decorative controls.</h2>
        <p>
          Precision tools are useful only when their visible feedback agrees with the document. Varve
          keeps target identity through snap evaluation, excludes moving hierarchies, avoids global
          integer rounding, and derives arrangement guides from the applied result. Numeric controls
          remain available when a drag or keyboard is not the right input method.
        </p>
        <a class="docs-link" href={sitePath('/docs/tools/precision-placement')}>Read the Precision Placement guide →</a>
      </section>
    </main>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .precision-page { max-width: 920px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 3rem 0 5rem; }
  .breadcrumb { color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: .875rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  .breadcrumb a { color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .page-hero { max-width: 720px; margin-bottom: 4rem; }
  .page-hero h1 { color: var(--text-primary); font: 700 clamp(2.4rem, 7vw, 4.7rem)/1.03 var(--font-editorial); letter-spacing: -.035em; margin: 1rem 0; }
  .page-hero p { color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 1.2rem; line-height: 1.7; }
  .eyebrow { color: var(--accent-primary); font-size: .75rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .hero-card, .why { border-radius: var(--website-radius-card); padding: clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem); }
  .hero-card { align-items: center; display: grid; gap: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 5rem); grid-template-columns: minmax(0, .9fr) minmax(360px, 1.1fr); margin-bottom: 5rem; }
  .hero-card h2, .capabilities h2, .why h2 { color: var(--text-primary); font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 3vw, 2.5rem); letter-spacing: -.02em; margin: .45rem 0 1rem; }
  .hero-card p:not(.eyebrow), .why p:not(.eyebrow) { color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.75; }
  .flow { align-items: stretch; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr; gap: var(--space-3); }
  .flow > div:not(.flow-arrow) { background: var(--surface-muted); border: 1px solid var(--border-default); border-radius: var(--website-radius-surface); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-2); padding: var(--space-4); }
  .flow .flow-accent { background: var(--surface-accent-soft); border-color: var(--border-accent); }
  .flow span { color: var(--text-tertiary); font-size: .7rem; }
  .flow strong { color: var(--text-primary); }
  .flow small { color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.4; }
  .flow-arrow { align-self: center; color: var(--accent-primary); font-size: 1.25rem; }
  .capabilities { margin-bottom: 5rem; }
  .capability-grid { display: grid; gap: var(--space-3); grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
  .capability-grid article { background: var(--surface-card); border: 1px solid var(--border-default); border-radius: var(--website-radius-surface); padding: var(--space-4); }
  .capability-grid h3 { color: var(--text-primary); font-size: 1rem; margin: 0 0 .5rem; }
  .capability-grid p { color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: .93rem; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0; }
  .why { background: var(--surface-muted); border: 1px solid var(--border-default); }
  .why p:not(.eyebrow) { max-width: 720px; }
  .docs-link { color: var(--text-link); display: inline-block; font-weight: 600; margin-top: var(--space-3); }
  @media (max-width: 780px) { .hero-card { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .capability-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }
  @media (max-width: 520px) { .precision-page { padding-top: 2rem; } .flow { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .flow-arrow { justify-self: start; transform: rotate(90deg); } .capability-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
